      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because this is a set and not a list, if the caller adds two identical requests, only one will be stored in the set. If later on one of the two is removed, neither of the requests will be stored in the set.\n\nIn the current code, can this happen? I\u0027m not sure it can, and in any case, the code before your CL uses a BitSet that likely has the same problem, right? If that\u0027s correct, then no issue here (but you could add a TODO).\n\nWhen we merge the CL that implements fuzzy matching (hopefully soon), will this continue not not be possible, because we\u0027ll never get two equal requests here? Or will we need to worry about this problem occurring when we merge that CL?",
      "range": {
